SWEET HID test key (patch 0398, oriole upstream port Step 8; applies after 0155): boot-arg sweethidtestkey=1 makes the existing sweethidtest=N timer (patch 0058/0155: a press every N s, sweethidcount presses) press consumer Volume Decrement instead of Menu, =2 Volume Increment; absent or any other value = Menu as before. The press goes through SweetHIDButtons::key -> dispatchEvent, the path of a real button (patch 0087), so a run can check what backboardd / SpringBoard / the audio path do with a volume key without a finger. No hardware access.

